      "text": "To solve the equation \\(\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)=12\\), let's first simplify the expression inside the parentheses.\n\nLet \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). The equation then becomes \\( y^2 + y = 12 \\). We can rewrite this as a quadratic equation:\n\n\\[ y^2 + y - 12 = 0 \\]\n\nThis quadratic equation can be factored as:\n\n\\[ (y + 4)(y - 3) = 0 \\]\n\nSo, the solutions for \\( y \\) are \\( y = -4 \\) or \\( y = 3 \\).\n\nNext, we need to find the corresponding values of \\( x \\). We have two cases to consider:\n\n1. \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4 \\)\n2. \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3 \\)\n\n**Case 1: \\( y = -4 \\)**\n\n\\[ \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4 \\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\) gives:\n\n\\[ 4x - 16 = -4(3x - 4) \\]\n\\[ 4x - 16 = -12x + 16 \\]\n\\[ 16x = 32 \\]\n\\[ x = 2 \\]\n\nWe need to verify if \\( x = 2 \\) is a valid solution by substituting it back into the original expression. When \\( x = 2 \\):\n\n\\[ \\frac{4(2)-16}{3(2)-4} = \\frac{8-16}{6-4} = \\frac{-8}{2} = -4 \\]\n\nSo, \\( x = 2 \\) is indeed a solution.\n\n**Case 2: \\( y = 3 \\)**\n\n\\[ \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3 \\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\) gives:\n\n\\[ 4x - 16 = 3(3x - 4) \\]\n\\[ 4x - 16 = 9x - 12 \\]\n\\[ -5x = 4 \\]\n\\[ x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\]\n\nWe need to verify if \\( x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\) is a valid solution by substituting it back into the original expression. When \\( x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\):\n\n\\[ \\frac{4\\left(-\\frac{4}{5}\\right) - 16}{3\\left(-\\frac{4}{5}\\right) - 4} = \\frac{-\\frac{16}{5} - 16}{-\\frac{12}{5} - 4} = \\frac{-\\frac{16}{5} - \\frac{80}{5}}{-\\frac{12}{5} - \\frac{20}{5}} = \\frac{-\\frac{96}{5}}{-\\frac{32}{5}} = \\frac{96}{32} = 3 \\]\n\nSo, \\( x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\) is also a solution.\n\nThe greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\( 2 \\), as it is larger than \\( -\\frac{4}{5} \\).\n\nTherefore, the greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
